    "title": "President Trump Announces Greenland Plan - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By B.D. Hobbs ,\n9 hours ago\nPresident Trump announced from Davos that he has formed the framework of a future deal with respect to Greenland and, in fact, the entire Arctic Region.\nIn a post on Truth Social, the President said, \" This solution, if consummated, will be a great one for the United States of America, and all NATO Nations.\"\nTrump added that he will not be imposing the Tariffs that were scheduled to go into effect on February 1st, and that additional discussions are being held concerning The Golden Dome as it pertains to Greenland.\nVice President JD Vance, Secretary of State Marco Rubio, Special Envoy Steve Witkoff, and various others, as needed, will be responsible for the negotiations, and will report directly to President Trump.\nFurther information will be made available as discussions progress.\nPhoto: Chip Somodevilla / Getty Images News / Getty Images 58",
